From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:29:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: CSE the address arithmetic before vectorizing loads
 and stores

nir_opt_load_store_vectorize only merges accesses whose offsets have the same
base SSA value. bifrost_postprocess_nir() runs it with nothing but copy
propagation before it, while the lowering earlier in the pass leaves one
copy of the address arithmetic per access: DXVK reads an instance- or
vertex-indexed constant buffer as index * stride + 16, + 20, + 24, + 28, each
access with its own index * stride. The four loads then have four different
bases and stay four LD_PKA.i32 instead of one LD_PKA.i128. Later passes CSE
the multiplications, but by then the vectorizer has run.

Run constant folding, algebraic optimizations, CSE and DCE right before the
vectorizer.

Tomb Raider (2013), DXVK, all 1218 graphics shaders of its benchmark run:
position shaders 103.8 -> 69.7 instructions and 27.4 -> 10.3 load/store
cycles on average, varying shaders 153.6 -> 112.0 and 39.4 -> 19.7,
fragment shaders 150.7 -> 148.5 and 15.9 -> 14.7. In the
disassembly 90% of the 32-bit UBO loads shared a 16-byte slot with another
load from the same base. Built-in benchmark 68.4 -> 74.0 / 74.3 fps
(stock Mali driver 71.8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: D3D performance: constant-buffer loads in DXVK/vkd3d shaders are vectorized (LD_PKA.i128 instead of four LD_PKA.i32); the load/store vectorizer only merges accesses with the same base SSA value and ran before the duplicated address arithmetic was CSE'd
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: applies after rg477m/046
Validation test: Tomb Raider (2013) built-in benchmark, DXVK 1.11.1, quietd Stock, uncapped, interleaved A C C A A C with the change env-gated in one build: 68.4 / 68.3 / 68.4 -> 74.0 / 74.3 / 73.8 fps (stock Mali driver 71.6 / 71.9); shader stats over its 1218 graphics shaders: position 27.4 -> 10.3 load/store cycles, varying 39.4 -> 19.7, fragment 15.9 -> 14.7; installed packages rg477m/001-047 compat a85fcca37a47 / unsafe 931e630faaba: Tomb Raider 74.5 / 73.3 fps; PanProbe compat 38/38 x2, unsafe 37/38 x2 (bc_decode by design); vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 suite 309 PASS, every test the same result as rg477m/001-045; 16-game boot sweep: every game in its known state, no GPU faults; gameplay A/B vs 001-046 compat (quietd Stock, uncapped): Hades hub 229.4 -> 228.0 fps (-0.6%), Jupiter Hell tutorial 47.7 -> 48.3, Risk of Rain 2 stage 1 27.1 -> 28.0 (map spread +-3), Serious Sam D3D11 bot benchmark 57.6 -> 57.3; DRG -dx12 renders (71 fps title)
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
index 4cab1dfa..fce2cd76 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
@@ -1121,6 +1121,16 @@ bifrost_postprocess_nir(nir_shader *nir,
    if (!(inputs->robust_modes & nir_var_mem_ssbo))
       vectorize_opts.modes |= nir_var_mem_ssbo;
 
+   /* The vectorizer only merges accesses whose offsets share a base SSA value.
+    * By now the lowering above has left one copy of the address arithmetic per
+    * access (each DXVK constant-buffer read computes its own index * stride),
+    * so contiguous scalar UBO loads would stay separate LD_PKA.i32. CSE first.
+    */
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_constant_folding);
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_algebraic);
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_cse);
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_dce);
+
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_load_store_vectorize, &vectorize_opts);
 
